  "plain": "On a podcast hosted by Jesse Michels, a guest named Merrick von Renenamp talks about AARO, the Pentagon office set up to look into reports of unexplained objects in the sky and elsewhere. He says that around 2024 the office had about three or four dozen staff, and that he had just heard it had reached \"full operational capability\", meaning it was fully up and running, and he credits a man named Jon Kosloski for this. It matters because the size of the office suggests how seriously the government takes these reports."
